  "csadapt-10041": "CarScanner embedded mqbadaptations.db (decoded via VAGCoder/tools/extract-carscanner-adaptations.py TLV layout) uid 10041 (FuelConsumptionCorrection, AD 2234, SBI0 DL1 MUL1 OFS0, VT1 input). min/max 85..115 % from the catalogue card range.",
  "csmqb-mqb-5-f-eco-driving": "VAGCoder/fixtures/private/coding-artifact-review/managed/CarScannerMaui.Coding.DB.MQB.Multimedia.decompiled.cs MQB_5F_EcoDriving (line 371): 0B3C enable 37.0=1,37.1=0,37.2=1,37.3=0 / disable all 0; 0B1B IsMIB3(): enable 35.7=1,35.6=0,35.5=1,35.4=0 / disable all 0, else enable 35.0=1,35.1=0,35.2=1,35.3=0 / disable all 0. Ordered first-match over 0B3C then 0B1B (MQBAlternativeCoding container order).",
  "group:show-offroad-screen-in-multimedia-system": "VAGCoder/fixtures/private/coding-artifact-review/managed/CarScannerMaui.Coding.DB.MQB.Multimedia.decompiled.cs MQB_5F_OffroadModeDisplayInMMI_Var2 (line 176): MQBMultipleCoding of 3 MQBAlternativeCoding parts, all applied. Part3 (mib25 0600 24.2 / mib3 0558 1.7 pwd 20103) is already a parsed field in the corpus. Vendor part3 has PostWriteCommands \"1102\" (ECU reset) which this contract has no key for. Container passwords are \"\" -> unit-5F default 20103 (vendor DefaultGetStateDelegate also forces 20103 on MIB3 773).",
  "csmqb-mqb-5-f-offroad-mode-display-in-mmi-var2-part1-p1": "VAGCoder/fixtures/private/coding-artifact-review/managed/CarScannerMaui.Coding.DB.MQB.Multimedia.decompiled.cs lines 178-218: container 0B3C enable 16.0=1,16.2=1 / disable 0,0; container 0B1B IsMIB3(): 16.7,16.5 = 1,1 / 0,0, else 16.0,16.2 = 1,1 / 0,0. Corpus had lost the 0B3C container and the 0B1B bytes.",
