  "dash-seat-belt-warning": "Alternatives on the cluster (unit 17): CarScanner embedded mqbadaptations.db (decoded via VAGCoder/tools/extract-carscanner-adaptations.py TLV layout) uid 10035 SeatBeltsAlerts AD 22B9 (ENABLE 00 / DISABLE 01; corpus password 47115) first, then uid 10136 SeatBeltsAlertsStyle 0600 b0 bits4..2 for clusters without 22B9 (DISABLE 000; \"enabled\" writes Ncap 001, the Euro style - restore from backup returns the car's own original style).",
  "dash-speed-warning": "CarScanner embedded mqbadaptations.db (decoded via VAGCoder/tools/extract-carscanner-adaptations.py TLV layout) uid 10087 SpeedWarning AD 228C BIT:0:0 (1 enable / 0 disable) + uid 10246 \"Speed warning: speed value\" AD 228C SBI1 DL1 MUL1 OFS0 (km/h) merged into one 228C ops write: Off clears 0.0 only; each preset sets 0.0=1 and byte1 = km/h (catalogue range 50..250).",
  "dash-speed-warning-india": "Alternatives on unit 17: live-cluster-speed-warning-india (0E46 byte0, enabled 0x31 / disabled 0x00, password 47115 live-proven on Kushaq 6JM920310) first; else Dashboard.cs MQB_17_WarningWhen120kmh (0600 SwitchBitInByte(array,0,6)) for clusters without 0E46. csadapt-10247 excluded (enable value 01 contradicts the live capture).",
  "dash-speed-limiter-activation": "CarScanner embedded mqbadaptations.db (decoded via VAGCoder/tools/extract-carscanner-adaptations.py TLV layout) uids 10323-10328 (\"Speed Limiter Activation: Step 1..6\"), all PWD 20103: step1 714/0AEA BIT:0:0, step2 714/0AEA BIT:0:2, step3 714/0AE7 BIT:0:0, step4 714/0E4F BIT:0:0, step5 757/0600 BIT:2:3+3:7, step6 757/0600 BIT:6:2 (label says U:01 but the DB record's RQH is 757, kept as recorded). Steps sharing a unit+DID are merged into one ops step so one backup/restore covers each DID. Audit 2026-11-03: steps 5/6 need unit 13 (757) to answer; cars without an ACC/distance module refuse at module identification before anything is written. The step-6 record is titled '(U:01)' but its RQH is 757; kept on 13 as the DB records it (no second source).",
  "steering-angle-display": "no-implementation (capture-required, low, probably absent): REMAINING_FEATURES #90 - no source; only a VCDS keyword lead ('Lenkwinkel' on 17). C# corpus / candidates / mqbadaptations.db hits are wheel heater, Wheel Circumference (10191) and steering-assist recipes - none is a cluster wheel-angle view.",
  "offroad-view-in-dashboard": "no-implementation (not-possible on MQB-A0-IN, low): REMAINING_FEATURES #86-88/#91 - Superb/Kodiaq/Tiguan Sport HMI, 4x4 or A5-camera only. C# corpus for Offroad|OffRoad (only MQB_5F_OffroadModeDisplayInMMI_Var2, a 5F MMI screen, used for offroad-information-screen); candidates + mqbadaptations.db for offroad (only 10249/10050 ambient-colour profiles). No unit-17 cluster offroad / wheel-angle view exists.",
  "speedometer-scale-range": "no-implementation (capture-required: channel high / DID med-guess): REMAINING_FEATURES #89 - 17 'Tachometer end value' versions 0..5 (Taigo CS: 0 default, 1=280, 2=240, 3=300, 4=260+, 5=280+), digital cluster only. The only DID lead is csadapt-10030 ActiveInfoDisplaySpeedometerStyle 17/0D60 byte0, options 00..0F with no labels; nothing ties its values to the end-value table, and the same lead is claimed by engine-speed-rpm-in-dashboard. Needs read 0D60 + VCDS diff on a digital cluster before mapping. C# corpus has no codingDB hit for Speedometer|Tacho|Scale|260|MaxSpeed.",
  "vehicle-path-display": "no-implementation (capture-required, low): REMAINING_FEATURES #92 - needs a 'high' rear-view camera unit 6C (gateway install list, 6C coding, 5F camera-type bits); the two forum sources disagree on byte numbers and no vendor routine touches 6C. Only RearCameraInstalled / camera washer / road-sign camera recipes exist.",
